---
import type { PublishedEvidence } from "../../data/releases/js-1.0-source";

interface Props {
  cases: PublishedEvidence["cases"];
}

const { cases } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="cases">
  <article>
    <header>
      <span class="case-tag">False-positive-shaped report</span>
      <h3>Tigerteam: SQL-shaped code without an executable sink</h3>
    </header>
    <p class="case-result">
      <strong>{cases.tigerteamSqlDecoyRuns} of 25 model runs reported the SQL-shaped decoy.</strong>
      The helper logs a string and returns an empty array; it never sends the
      constructed query to a database.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`function dbQuery(sql) {
  console.log("Query:", sql);
  return [];
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      This is the kind of vulnerability-shaped pattern an LLM can describe
      plausibly even when the required execution sink is absent.
    </p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <header>
      <span class="case-tag likely-gap">Likely product-gap candidate</span>
      <h3>Nightowl: unmatched SQL injection with a real database sink</h3>
    </header>
    <p class="case-result">
      <strong>{cases.nightowlSqlGapRuns} of 25 model runs reported the likely SQL injection gap.</strong>
      Unlike Tigerteam, this helper concatenates an identifier into an
      executable SQLite statement.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`deleteTodo: (id) =>
  db.prepare("DELETE FROM todos WHERE id = " + id).all()`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      It remained unmatched because it was outside the Snyk Code reference
      set. That status should trigger investigation, not automatic dismissal.
    </p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <header>
      <span class="case-tag systematic-gap">Systematic coverage gap</span>
      <h3>Nightowl: stable output can still be incomplete</h3>
    </header>
    <p class="case-result">
      Claude Opus 4.6 High held a stable 40.0% Snyk-reference F1 while missing
      <strong>{cases.nightowlPathTraversalMisses} of 15 path-traversal opportunities</strong>
      and <strong>{cases.nightowlResourceLimitMisses} of 15 resource-limit opportunities</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The model recognized representative high-signal issues but did not
      enumerate repeated vulnerable sinks as systematically as deterministic
      SAST.
    </p>
  </article>
</div>

<style>
  .cases {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }

  article {
    display: grid;
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  header {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .case-tag {
    width: fit-content;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--unmatched);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .case-tag.likely-gap {
    border-color: var(--matched);
  }

  .case-tag.systematic-gap {
    border-color: var(--warning);
  }

  h3 {
    max-width: 34rem;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  p {
    max-width: 50rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .case-result {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .case-result strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  pre {
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border-left: 0.25rem solid var(--purple);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper-raised);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (min-width: 58rem) {
    article {
      grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
      column-gap: var(--space-7);
    }

    article > :not(header) {
      grid-column: 2;
    }

    article header {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 1 / span 4;
      align-content: start;
    }
  }
</style>
